      "writtenOn": "2021-09-15T12:05:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LGTM. BTW, the requirements for RpcPreconnectedClient would be:\n\n1) RpcPreconnectedClient is a function having C ABI.\n2) A caller can pass any functions, holding any wanted contexts, to RpcConnectedClient.\n\nI\u0027ve done 2) by letting clients pass a void* parameter to which they can store their own contexts, but it seems to force Rust clients to use unsafe. Can we achieve 1) and 2) without the need of unsafe in Rust?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "5ab57979e6aa34522b554b9974b6781c773f664a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
